\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia says reserves not hurt by rupiah fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 1996\par 09:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 9 (Reuter) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Tuesday that the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were not hurt by last week's fall in the rupiah on concerns over President Suharto's health. \par \par \uc2  "The recent speculation has not had any impact on our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. Total trading last Thursday was relatively small," Governor Sudradjad Djiwandono told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah plunged to a year-low of 2,349 to the dollar on Thursday following unfounded rumours that Suharto had suffered a heart attack. \par \par \uc2  It has since stabilised and was trading at 2,339.00 on Tuesday afternoon. The government has said Suharto is in good health but is currently in Germany for three days of medical checks which are slated to begin today. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market despite the fall, because even after the drop the rupiah was well within the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, Sudradjad said. \par \par \uc2  He added that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue its prudent policies to maintain the confidence of foreign investors in the country's economy. \par \par \uc2  Official sources said last week Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves had risen to $16.483 billion in June from $15.914 billion in May. \par \par \uc2  "What Bank Indonesia can do is continuously show our macro- economic consistency. We will continue our prudent monetary policy, including controlling inflation and the dollar-rupiah exchange rate," Sudradjad said. \par \par \uc2  He said those steps in addition to a prudent loan policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve management would lead to a healthy current account. \par \par \uc2  Sudradjad also said Bank Indonesia has taken steps to curb fluctuations in the exchange rate, including maintaining relatively large reserves and coordinating action with other central banks. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, speaking at the opening of an international seminar on the 50th anniversary of Bank BNI 1946, Sudradjad said restructuring the banking industry was a high priority of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We will continue to encourage banks to merge as a part of restructuring. The mergers between banks are likely to increase their competitiveness," he said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds7905lh9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
