\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Flat Vs. Dlr; Slow Mkt Lacking News \b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1996\par 05:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah is flat versus the U.S. dollar in extremely slow trading early Tuesday as the market waits for market-moving news in an amply liquid market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also say that the market has accommodated itself to the new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading band unveiled Thursday by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was widened to 118 rupiah from 66 rupiah, and its conversion band was widened to 46 rupiah from 44. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is being bought at 2,322.37 rupiah in the spot market at 0319 GMT Tuesday after starting the day at 2,322.50 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  'It is a very dull in the market today, with nothing moving the spot or forward markets either way,' said a dealer at a foreign bank. 'Yesterday's liquidity was tight, so the dollar has moved up a bit on improved conditions, but outside of that there's nothing.' \par \par \uc2  Because of this languid environment, traders see the dollar trading in an extremely tight range of between 2,322 rupiah and 2,323 rupiah Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say, however, that the dollar should move up a bit later in the week as people seek dollar-funding to pay off overseas obligations. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-06-96 \par \par \uc2  0354GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds6i04zan\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
