\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia moves to curb capital inflow. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, June 14 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah surged against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened its dollar-rupiah trading band in an attempt to stem the inflow of speculative funds, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But they were unsure whether the move was potent enough because highly attractive domestic interest rates could continue to be a magnet for foreign funds. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday widened its dollar-rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to 118 rupiah or five percent at 2,315/2,433 rupiah to the dollar from 66 rupiah or three percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when the exchange rate goes outside the parameters. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is wise to widen it now. It shows the rupiah market is getting more and more mature, which allows the market to decide the exchange rate," Edwin Png, chief treasurer of Bank of America in Jakarta told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The move took the market by surprise and sent the dollar tumbling even though the broadening had been long-expected by players because of bullish sentiment on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "The market has become more mature as of yesterday. There was some support (for the dollar) and operators did not sell the dollar down to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's base rate," Png said. \par \par \uc2  "The market forces somehow determined what is the best exchange rate. That is a good sign," he added. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia said the move was aimed at curbing the inflow of speculative funds and increasing its monetary control. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to absorb dollars, estimated at a total of some $800 million, from the market three times in the past two weeks after the dollar hit its floor rate. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the absorption induced fresh rupiah supply which threatened the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's broad M2 money supply aggregate, which is targeted to grow 17 percent for 1996/97 (April-March) fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  M2 year-on-year growth in April was 30 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were unsure whether the band move would help reduce short-term inflows as interest rate differentials between the dollar and the rupiah were in favour of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Pardy Kendy, chief treasurer of PT Bank Buana Indonesia, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was caught in the dilemma of controlling money supply growth while narrowing interest rate differentials. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the rupiah offered some 2.5 percent gains for investors, assuming the interest rate differential of the rupiah to the dollar at about eight percent and a rupiah depreciation of around 5.5 percent annually. \par \par \uc2  "It's a fantastic amount," Kendy said. \par \par \uc2  He said interest rate cuts to narrow the difference would be difficult because it would trigger another round of credit growth which the bank was now trying to control. \par \par \uc2  "It's a difficult dilemma. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to reduce short-term capital inflows while bringing the money supply down to an acceptable level," Kendy said. \par \par \uc2  Economists had suggested the possibility of a hike in the reserve requirement rate to curb money supply growth. \par \par \uc2  But Kendy said a hike in the reserve rate would invite further capital inflows because of higher interest rates, although it may help tighten credit growth. \par \par \uc2  "It's not an easy job. It's not to be envied," one said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds6e06p8h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
