\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia/ \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 /Band -3:Dissuade Speculative Money \b0\par\par\uc2 172 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 1996\par 12:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The distance between the lower end of the trading band and the higher end now is 5%, compared to 3% previously. \par \par \uc2  Djiwandono said the reason why the trading band was widened is to encourage the inflow of long-term funds, instead of the 'speculative medium-and short-term money.' \par \par \uc2  Djiwandono added that by widening the band more transactions will be done between banks with minimized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will make it easier to maintain the stability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, and to a larger extent, the monetary stability, the governor said. \par \par \uc2  A director with Bank Indonesia, Paul Soetopo, added that wider trading bands has increased the trading volume. He mentioned that when the spread of the trading band was six rupiah in 1991, the averaged daily trading volume was only $6 million. But when the spread of the band was 66 rupiah the average trading volume reached $5 billion per day. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-06-96 \par \par \uc2  1052GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds6d04vxb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
