\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Indonesia widens dollar-rupiah trading band. \b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, June 13 (Reuter) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said on Thursday it had widened the dollar-rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to 118 rupiah, or five percent, from 66 rupiah or three percent previously. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the conversion band remained unchanged at two percent, or 46 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "To increase the effectivity of monetary management and to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate due to rising capital flows it is necessary to proceed with the policy," the bank said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  It said the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should be able to accomodate supply and demand from local and overseas. \par \par \uc2  "This should reduce pressure on the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and should help increase monetary stability and foreign reserves," the bank said. \par \par \uc2  The new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was at 2,315/2,433 rupiah to the dollar, and the conversion band was fixed at 2,315.0/2,361.0. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if the exchange rate goes outside the perimeters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the managed floating rate of the rupiah through a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be maintained. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah rose sharply against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  broadened its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah touched a high of 2,320.0 from 2,336.0 before the dollar managed to rebound to 2,327.5/28.0 late in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer said the move had surprised the market although it had been widely anticipated. \par \par \uc2  "There was no quote immediately after the widening. The dollar suddenly tumbled to 2,330 and fell all the way down to a low 2,320.0," one European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Operators keep saying 'yours' all the time whatever price you quoted. It'a a bit drastic," he added. \par \par \uc2  However, he said the dollar rebounded gradually and could stabilise at around the 2,327/28.0 level. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer said it was not clear where the rate would head on Friday, but the liquidity condition could become the factor to look at in the short-term. \par \par \uc2  The fall of the dollar after the broadening of the band was in line with market expectations because the market was bullish on the rupiah before the long-anticipated move was realised. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds6d06n6g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
