\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian economy seen gaining confidence. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1996\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, June 4 (Reuter) - Indonesian money supply has risen above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target, while inflation remains under control, indicating increased confidence in the fast-developing economy, economists said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But they said an overshooting of money aggregates might strengthen market speculation of an imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move to widen its dollar-rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  Economists said foreign investors were pouring money into the country, which expects economic growth of around seven percent this year, against 8.07 percent in 1995. \par \par \uc2  "It comes as no surprise to us. It's an unwritten approval that investors have confidence in the economy," JP Morgan economist Vincent Low told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's consumer price index for May was expected to rise by between 0.05 and 0.07 percent, against 0.78 percent in April, banking sources told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Year-on-year inflation in April was 7.95 percent, against 8.86 percent in March 1996, and 10.02 percent in April 1995. \par \par \uc2  Economists attributed the decrease to an easing in prices of key consumer goods, after the first quarter index was hit by a rise in public transport fares in March and the Moslem Eid al-Fitr and Chinese Lunar new year holidays in February. \par \par \uc2  They said that year-on-year growth of the broad money aggregate, M2, was 30 percent in April, against 28 percent in March. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sudradjad Djiwandono said last month that M2 growth needed to be curbed. Indonesia aims for M2 growth of 17 percent for 1996/97 (April-March). \par \par \uc2  "I think it's suggesting that our economy is growing at a fast pace, reflected by rising M2. It seems other indicators are under control," Pardi Kendy, chief treasurer of PT Bank Buana Indonesia, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "I believe the money supplies were being driven by two sources, official foreign reserves and loans growth," JP Morgan's Low said. \par \par \uc2  Economists said rising foreign capital inflow, both short and longer-term, seemed to have helped boost reserves. \par \par \uc2  Short-term inflow was driven by an attractive interest rate differential offered by the rupiah, while the longer-term inflow came from soaring foreign investments as confidence in the economy continued to grow. \par \par \uc2  "Official foreign reserves have been rising quite quickly. It's a pretty rapid reserve accumulation," Low said. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose steadily to $15.961 billion in April from $14.789 billion in January. \par \par \uc2  "What you see in the reserve figure is also being reflected in the strength of the rupiah. It's trading at a very strong end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) band," Low said. \par \par \uc2  One senior economist suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might again widen the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band for dollar-rupiah trading, having broadened it to three percent last December. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at 2,332.75 to the dollar on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The World Bank said in its latest report on \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  that higher reserve requirements and a wider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band could increase the effectiveness of monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if market rates move out of the range. \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have to widen the band. Otherwise, it would have to absorb dollars from the market, which would in turn induce fresh inflows. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds64074gc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
