\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Indonesian newspapers - June 4. \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  Following is a summary of major Indonesian political and business stories in leading newspapers, prepared by Reuters in Jakarta. Reuters has not checked the stories and does not guarantee their accuracy. Telephone: (6221) 384-6364. Fax: (6221) 344-8404. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  KOMPAS \par \par \uc2  The government has given the opposition Indonesian Democratic Party (PDI) permission to hold a party congress soon, the director general of the Home Affairs and Sociopolitics Ministry said. He said this was an opportunity for the PDI to solve its internal problems concerning the party's leadership. \par \par \uc2  Personal interest or traditional laws should not interfere with government plans to conduct a government land appropriation programme, Indonesia's Vice-President Try Sutrisno said. He referred to problems over reallocation of land involving local people and the government. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA POST \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Indonesia, has drafted a new ruling on bank liquidation to provide better protection for depositors, bank governor J. Sudradjad Djiwandono said. He explained that existing rules on liquidation of limited liability companies were very general in nature. \par \par \uc2  More open forums and dialogue where people can release their frustration in an orderly and civilized manner are needed to resolve mounting social unrest, the speaker of the House of Representatives, Wahono, said. He said the government's excessive fear of increasing political openness might heighten tension and result in unjustified violence. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  REPUBLIKA \par \par \uc2  Minister of Industry and Trade Tunky Ariwibowo will meet head of the Bimantara Group, Bambang Trihatmodjo, a son of President Suharto. They will discuss plans of Bimantara's subsidiary, PT Citramobil National, to develop its own national car without tariff and tax breaks. So far, only PT Timor Putra Nasional, controlled by Bambang's brother Hutomo Mandala Putra, has been given such breaks to develop a national car. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  BISNIS INDONESIA \par \par \uc2  Economists said it is the right time for Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to widen the spread of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in order to reduce speculation in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions amidst fears of a rising account deficit. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds64074ai\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
