\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia seen squeezing money supply growth. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 1996\par 12:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, May 30 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may broaden its dollar-rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band and raise reserve requirements for banks to clamp down on money supply growth, economists said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  One economist said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , might move again to widen the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band for dollar-rupiah trading after broadening it to three percent, or 66 points (rupiah to the dollar), last December. \par \par \uc2  The bank can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when market rates move out of the range the bank fixes on a daily basis. \par \par \uc2  The economist said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might also consider raising the reserve requirement, last raised in February to three percent from two percent, to curtail new loans. \par \par \uc2  JP Morgan said in its May report that Bank Indonesia would probably attempt to restrict credit through regulatory measures and a further increase in the reserve requirement. \par \par \uc2  "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to take action on the band again. But I don't know when," the economist said. There was no official comment from the bank. \par \par \uc2  "There is a distinct possibility the band will be widened. It will be good for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take some steam off the market," said Winston Koh, of JP Morgan in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Koh said a wider band was in line with Bank Indonesia's policy that the dollar-rupiah rate moved toward a free-float within the band itself. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sudradjad Djiwandono said last week that the growth of M2 money supply needed to be curbed. \par \par \uc2  Djiwandono said that although growth in M1 showed indications of slowing since the third quarter of 1995, broad M2 money supply remained high. M2 growth was 26.79 percent in the year to February 1996, compared with 28.04 percent in the year to November 1995. \par \par \uc2  The 1996/97 (April-March) state budget set an M2 growth target of 17 percent. \par \par \uc2  Djiwandono said strong credit demand was responsible for high M2 growth. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said high domestic interest rates had attracted capital inflow, which had complicated monetary management and kept the dollar under pressure for several months. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to widen the band because otherwise it has to absorb dollars from the market, which could undermine its money supply target. Dollar-buying will induce fresh funds in the market," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said the band might be broadened before a rise in the reserve rate because Bank Indonesia might wait to see the full impact of February's reserve increase. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said speculation about a possible change in the band would put the dollar under further pressure in anticipation that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might continue easing within a broader band. \par \par \uc2  They said the dollar had softened in response to past widenings of the band. \par \par \uc2  "It's just a question of time when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be forced to absorb dollars from the market, because sentiment on the rupiah has been strong. It could be the right timing again," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band on Thursday was fixed at 2,331.0/2,397 and the conversion rate at 2,331.0/2,375.0. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds5u07bhq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
