\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Tjokronegoro -3: Must 1st Consider Existing Groups \b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 1996\par 04:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Tjokronegoro noted that the Mexican peso crisis caused a speculative ripple in the Indonesian rupiah and despite dire forecasts by private economists on the outlook for Indonesian economy, the rupiah has held up quite well. He said the repo agreements are a means of ensuring that central banks can continue to defend against speculative attacks. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market several times following the Mexican peso crisis to keep the rupiah within its trading band. \par \par \uc2  Tjokronegoro said he is aware of a push for formalized cooperation along the lines of the Basel-based Bank for International Settlements (BIS), but said strong thought should be given to strengthening existing regional groups before proceeding further. \par \par \uc2  He noted that there are already roughly a dozen regional organizations to which Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  belongs and said he worries about the overlapping responsibility and reduced efficiency if yet another organization is created. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-04-96 \par \par \uc2  0207GMT \par \par \uc2  4230 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds450311y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
