\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah stable in slow late Jakarta trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Feb 15 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was stable against the dollar in late trading, dealers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  They said sentiment on dollars remained bearish despite relatively sufficient rupiah supply in the money market. \par \par \uc2  One foreign bank dealer said the market appeared to be calm ahead of the last trading day on Friday before leaving for an extended weekend untill next Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  He said operators seemed to speculate a more relaxed money market on Friday because of an anticipated injection from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of at least $500 million equivalent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed from February 19 to 21 and the stock market from February 19 to 23 for the Eid al-Fitr celebrations. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was last at 2,96.0/96.5, compared with an opening of 2,296.25/96.75. Tomorrow was at 2,292.90/93.15. \par \par \uc2  Today rupiah closed at 2,291.50/92.00. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said offshore players tended to push the rupiah lower in the past when the local market closed for long holidays. \par \par \uc2  "I don't know whether this may happen again because Eid al-Fitr happens to be at the same time as the Lunar New Year." \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was at 0.6/0.8 and tom/next at 3.10/3.15. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the dollar-rupiah rate was likely to range around 2,296.0 and 2,298.0 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at 2,294/2,360 and the conversion rate at 2,294/2,338 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  One-month swap was at 17.75/18.50, two at 38.75/39.00, three at 58.75/58.90 and six at 118.0/119.0. \par \par \uc2  -- Mantik Kusjanto, Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2f01ibp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
