\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia:Rupiah Dn Vs Dlr;Short Covering Before Weekend \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 1996\par 05:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's rupiah weakened slightly versus the U.S. dollar in fairly quiet trading early Friday as some participants covered their dollar-short positions ahead of the weekend, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit is being bought at 2,293.25 rupiah in the spot market at 0355 GMT Friday, up from its opening level at 2,292.50 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  A dealer said rupiah liquidity is ample Friday after banks sold the dollar to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Indonesia, for the last two days. \par \par \uc2  'However, it (ample liquidity) doesn't help the dollar a lot as people are anticipating healthy demand for the rupiah during the Lebaran, and Chinese New Year holidays,' said Trisiladi Supriyanto, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at PT Indosuez Indonesia Bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's surge versus the yen does not affect the dollar-rupiah trading level directly. But it affects it indirectly because Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  raises its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band if the dollar rises against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers see the dollar remaining trapped in a narrow range of 2,292.75 rupiah and 2,293.75 rupiah Friday in the absence of any fresh news that could move trading. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to be tied to the floor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in the first days of next week as good demand for the rupiah from domestic and overseas players is seen unflagging. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0414GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 \par 