\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia: Rupiah Flat Vs Dollar In Quiet Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 1996\par 04:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-DJ)--Indonesia's rupiah was little changed against the U.S. dollar in quiet trading early Thursday as dealers were reluctant to take positions because of the narrow trading range, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 2,291.67 rupiah in the spot market at 0244 GMT Thursday, rebounding from its intraday low of 2,291.37 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said local banks bought the dollar since it is close to the dollar bids of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. When the dollar hits the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, local banks can sell the dollar to Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, overseas banks were still keen to selling the dollar on higher yields provided by the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  'The downward pressure on the dollar remains intact,' said Yayang Wijaya, a dealer at PT Bank Mitsubishi Buana. Wijaya expects the strong gain on the Jakarta Stock Exchange (JSX) early Thursday to put more weight on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0244 GMT Thursday the JSX index rose 1.2%, or 6.897 points, following a 1.6% increase Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Market players see the dollar Thursday remaining tied up in the narrow range between 2,291 rupiah and 2,292 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Weekend short covering is expected to alleviate the dollar to a higher level between 2,292 rupiah and 2,293 rupiah Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 31-01-96 \par \par