\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia central bank \highlight\uc2  sets  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  rate. \b0\par\par\uc2 121 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 2 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , set its first dollar/rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate on Tuesday at 2,278/2,344. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced last Friday a three-percent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band for dollar-rupiah trading that became effective on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The new three percent, or 66 points, band allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when the market rate moves out of the band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed its conversion rate at 2,278/2,322 on Tuesday, compared with 2,286/2,330 last Friday. The bank was closed on Monday for the New Year holiday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds1203adx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
