\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  sets  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  band for  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  trading. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1995\par 10:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Dec 29 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band for dollar-rupiah trading on Friday aimed at increasing the effectiveness of monetary controls and maintaining a stable exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia set a new band of three percent or 66 points (rupiah to the dollar) which would allow it to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when the market rate moves 1.5 percent up or down. \par \par \uc2  "To improve the effectiveness of monetary control and the stability of the exchange rate in order to anticipate future growth of capital flow, we see the need to further develop the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Paul Soetopo, managing director of Bank Indonesia, told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  Soetopo said the move was also aimed at reducing pressure on the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. The rupiah strengthened to 2,284.0/89.0 to the dollar from Thursday's closing at 2,291.50/92.0 in the Singapore market, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The managed floating system which is based on a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and has become the central mechanism to calculate the exchange rate of the rupiah will be maintained," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said the conversion rate band of two percent - one percent up or down - or 44 points, fixed by Bank Indonesia on a daily basis, remained unchanged. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar conversion rate on Friday was fixed at 2,286/2,330 to the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  A Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Reuters the new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band would be the range which allows banks to buy or sell dollars with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the authority to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at any time, even when the dollar-rupiah rate was within the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  The conversion rate is the rate for export drafts and other transactions with government bodies. \par \par \uc2  The official said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would consider on a case-by-case basis when commercial banks wanted to buy/sell dollars with Bank Indonesia when the market rate was within the zone between the conversion and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bands. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will announce the conversion and the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates at 3.00 p.m. (0800 GMT) every trading day. \par \par \uc2  Soetopo also announced on Friday a set of measures to regulate derivatives trading. Soetopo said the rules, effective from Friday, permit banks to carry out derivatives transactions related only to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "Derivatives transactions in shares would be approved by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a case-by-case basis," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said derivatives trading should be based on healthy and prudent principles and such trades must be approved by banks' board of commissioners and directors. \par \par \uc2  Soetopo said maximum loss exposure should not exceed 10 percent of a bank's capital while derivatives trading resulting from a customer's order could cover up to 10 times his margin deposits placed with a bank. \par \par \uc2  He said banks are also obliged to give a detailed explanation of the risks involved in derivatives trading. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had widened the spread of dollar buying/selling four times since 1992. \par \par \uc2  It said the moves had helped develop the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and reduced the dependency on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading volume has risen to $4.6 billion a day in 1995, compared with $2.7 billion daily in 1992 while transactions with Bank Indonesia declined to $24 million a day from $37 million in the same period. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drct009ky\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
