\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia/Conversion Rate -3:Managed Floating Rate Policy \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1995\par 07:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  This new regulation will go into effect on Jan. 2, 1996, Paul Sutopo added. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director stated that Bank Indonesia is committed to continuing its 'managed floating notes policy' which is calculated through a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'This mechanism has been very effective in controlling the rupiah's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations,' he said, denying opinions voiced by analysts recently that the rupiah has been overvalued by 16%. \par \par \uc2  Sutopo also stated that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates will continue to be calculated through a market oriented mechanism. \par \par \uc2  He concluded by saying that 'the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchasing rates should not be higher than the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band while the buying rates can't be lower than the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band.' \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transaction volume has risen to $4.6 billion per year in 1995, up from $2.7 billion per day four years earlier in 1992. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transaction volume between Bank Indonesia and commerical banks has decreased to $24 million per day at the end of 1995, from $37 million per day in 1992. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-12-95 \par \par \uc2  0646GMT \par \par \uc2  CORRECTED AT 0214 EST \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drct0a6yj\par }\page {\