\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Rupiah/Showdown -2: Rupiah May Resist Weakening \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 1995\par 02:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  If Bank Indonesia continues to weaken the rupiah through its fixing, but the rupiah remains strong in the spot market in November and December, the dollar could fall through the bottom of the trading band and prompt Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers say, as it has in the past. In December 1994, Bank Indonesia entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and bought dollars to accelerate the rupiah depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The question being asked in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  desks in Jakarta and the region is: will \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets go along with the depreciation of the rupiah? And if monetary authorities want a weaker rupiah, when will they start to push down the rupiah fixing? \par \par \uc2  Daniel Lian, a regional economist with NatWest Markets in Singapore, believes \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players have no choice but to go along with a \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  induced depreciation. Bank Indonesia will get its way and depreciate the rupiah versus the dollar by 5% this year, Lian said. \par \par \uc2  'If Bank Indonesia raises the (dollar) fixing, I don't think people will bet on the rupiah and try to get in the way of depreciation,' Lian said. \par \par \uc2  However, other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players believe the market won't see the rupiah depreciate that much without a fight. \par \par \uc2  'Although the downward pressure on the dollar will ease when Telkom's share offering is over, the dollar's rise versus the rupiah will be curbed by the still healthy demand for the rupiah, because of high interest rates in rupiah-denominated paper,' said Trisiladi Supriyanto, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager with PT Indosuez Indonesia Bank. \par \par \uc2  In 1994 Bank Indonesia only managed a depreciation of 2.7%, and in 1993 only 2.2% versus the dollar, both below the annual 3%-5% target. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-10-95 \par \par \uc2  0041GMT \par \par \uc2  1190 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025draj084wj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
