\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Indonesia Gov/Exchange Rate Policy -3:No Policy Shifts \b0\par\par\uc2 132 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 1995\par 11:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  At present, Bank Indonesia has set a 44-rupiah band for dollar-rupiah trading in the spot market, between which trading is expected. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  every time the dollar-rupiah trading strays outside the band. \par \par \uc2  Soedradjad said recent pressure on the exchange rate has generally been related to speculative capital inflows, which were transitory, and 'require no major policy adjustment.' \par \par \uc2  Swap transactions (by Bank Indonesia) recently were discontinued in order to help the development of a reliable domestic interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Soedradjad said. \par \par \uc2  'In addition, the volume of transactions on the domestic interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is more than sufficient to facilitate swap without participation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' Soedradjad said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-10-95 \par \par \uc2  0940GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dra407oqf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
