\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah -2: Fixing Seen Up One Rupiah Monday \b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1995\par 10:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The dollar took off versus the rupiah Monday on the wings of a large Singapore bank agressively buying dollars in the Jakarta market. Early trading was moderate and local banks immediately followed the lead of offshore banks by covering their dollar-short positions. \par \par \uc2  That led the dollar on an upward spiral to near the ceiling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-rupiah 44-rupiah wide trading band at 2,285 rupiah, which prompted fears of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar selling. \par \par \uc2  Further powering the dollar were unconfirmed rumors whispered from Singapore but discounted by Jakarta veterans that Bank Indonesia would discard the dollar-rupiah trading band and let the rupiah be an absolute free-float \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to stabilize at around 2,270 rupiah for the rest of Monday with topside resistance at 2,285 rupiah, the ceiling of the dollar-rupiah trading band. Market players expect Bank Indonesia will raise the dollar-rupiah fixing by one rupiah to 2,242 rupiah - 2,286 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0804GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8l06c54\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
