\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Move May Prompt  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia Intervention \highlight\uc2 : Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By Peter Halesworth \par \uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1995\par 08:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar finally tackled the elusive and strong rupiah Monday and eased concerns that the rupiah might become overvalued, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players said. \par \par \uc2  However, the dollar's agressive move up Monday, when it reached a high of 2,279 rupiah from its opening at 2,250 rupiah, may have been even a bit extreme for Indonesia's monetary authorities, who want to see the rupiah depreciate versus the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but gradually and in an orderly manner. \par \par \uc2  'The movement of the market today is abnormal,' said a dealer at an Indonesian state bank in Jakarta who declined to be identified. 'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not happy. They want this done step-by-step. But a sudden movement can do things they do not want to see.' \par \par \uc2  In a volatile day of moderate trading whose cause mystified market players, many are speculating about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next move. Many expect that if the dollar rally is overdone, Bank Indonesia will move in and sell the U.S. unit as early as the afternoon fixing at around 0730 GMT Monday. \par \par \uc2  'Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  if a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is unjustified,' said Daniel Lian, regional economist for NatWest Markets in Singapore. 'One of these days they should come in. They certainly won't let the dollar go above the band.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JO