\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asia Ctrl Banks/Mexico -3: Singapore Did Not  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 1995\par 08:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  report stated that as international fund managers in January withdrew their money from emerging markets in Asia, stock markets began to decline and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened under considerable selling pressure. \par \par \uc2  'To calm the instability in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, several Asian emerging-market nations took steps towards increased security, primarily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' the report stated. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  defended the exchange rate of the Thai baht through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and by guaranteeing there would be no devaluation off the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the report said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also opened a swap facility for foreign banks with a premium of as much as 9% per year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and also raised interest rates, while Hong Kong and Malaysia only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the report said. \par \par \uc2  'Singapore, as a nation with a relatively stable economy, did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the weakness of the Singapore dollar was still within reasonable limits,' the report said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-07-95 \par \par \uc2  0630GMT \par \par \