\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Firms Vs Dlr After Early Storm Offshore \b0\par\par\uc2 214 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1995\par 04:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-DJ)--Offshore banks unloaded rupiah in early, volatile trade Monday as the yen's march ignited fears about Indonesia's ability to pay its yen-dominated debt, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Local banks, however, stemmed the rupiah's fall, showing more confidence in Indonesia's economic fundamentals despite jitters abroad and stabilizing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar is being bought at 2,233.65 rupiah on the spot market, down from its early Monday high of 2,235.50 rupiah but up from its low of 2,233.75 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Singapore banks reacted to the yen's new high versus the U.S. Dollar of 86.47 yen with knee-jerk selling of the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  'There is a major concern here about Indonesia's high debt burden in yen,' said Daniel Lian of NatWest Bank in Singapore. 'When the U.S. Dollar collapses, banks in Singapore are eager to sell the rupiah and buy dollars.' \par \par \uc2  The local market nervously waited early Monday for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar selling by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the dollar ignored its ceiling of 2,234 rupiah to buy the dollar, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not stir. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-04-95 \par \par \uc2  0247GMT \par \par \uc2  1159 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4302bo9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
