\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian Central Banks/Hotline -2: Indonesia Details Moves \b0\par\par\uc2 160 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 08:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Speculators launched attacks on several \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in mid-January. Monetary authorities in the region restored calm, some through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, to defend their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a total of $500 million defending the rupiah on January 12 and 13, Soedradjad said. \par \par \uc2  Representatives of the six nations then gathered on January 21 in Hong Kong with the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to discuss future regional cooperation against speculators. \par \par \uc2  Soedradjad also gave legislators Tuesday a rare account of how Bank Indonesia's moves in January helped squash speculators' hopes for devaluation of the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Rumors of devaluation of the rupiah started after Mexico devalued its peso by 15% on December 20. Poor investor sentiment towards emerging markets soon spread to Asia. \par \par \uc2  Between January 11 and 12, the U.S. Dollar rose sharply to 2,217 rupiah from 2,202 rupiah, Soedradjad said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-03-95 \par \par \uc2  0714GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3l021ad\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
