\par\par \b \uc2  Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: To Mute Speculation \b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 05:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-DJ)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Indonesia, sold around 100 million dollars Wednesday at the 'one-month' market to drive the dollar down versus the rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank Indonesia sold the dollar when the dollar reached around 2,225.50 rupiah at the spot market, and was successful in sending the U.S. unit down to 2,220.50 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia was not available for immediate confirmation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at muting the speculation on the rupiah devaluation against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar jumped to its high at 2,225 rupiah Wednesday on the spot market from its opening at 2,216 rupiah on devaluation speculation. \par \par \uc2  Overseas players speculated that Indonesia may be forced to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar in the wake of the yen's surge, as around 40% of Indonesia's foreign debt is in the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-03-95 \par \par \uc2  0444GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3801mjh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
