\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia's Jan. Foreign Reserves -2: Up 4.5% Vs Yr Ago \b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 1995\par 09:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-DJ)--Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in January slipped $185 million to $12.972 billion from December, a Bank Indonesia official said Monday. \par \par \uc2  The decrease is mainly due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sold a total $500 million to defend the value of the rupiah against the U.S. unit in the aftermath of Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis, the official said. \par \par \uc2  It is the third consecutive monthly decrease after three months of increases. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in January rose 4.5% from a year ago, when the total was $12.419 billlion, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's foreign reserves are expected to continue rising this year. Bank Indonesia Governor J. Soedradjad Djiwandono said earlier in January that Indonesia's foreign reserves are projected to gain during fiscal year 1995-96, starting April 1, by $1.800 billion to $15.500 billion by March 31, 1996. \par \par \uc2  That is enough to finance five months of imports, Soedradjad added. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-02-95 \par \par \uc2  0842GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr2d00v48\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
