\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia says no plan to reschedule foreign debt. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Muklis Ali \par \uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 16 (Reuter) - Indonesian President Suharto on Monday said the country has no plan to reschedule its foreign debt, which has hit almost $100 billion and triggered fears of a Mexican-style financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  "We have never thought to reschedule our foreign debt and there is no reason to reschedule it. Our foreign debt is in a safe position," State Secretary Murdiono quoted Suharto as saying when he meet with reporters at the Presidential palace. \par \par \uc2  "Our foreign debt is being handled well," Suharto said. \par \par \uc2  The comments from Suharto, an ex-army general credited with helping rescue Indonesia from near economic chaos after he took over in the late 1960s, coincided with moves by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike key discount rates on Monday to boost the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets were hit last week by investor nervousness that Indonesia's foreign debt level could trigger a Mexican-style devaluation. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market earlier on Monday appeared to have stabilised after Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market last week totalling $500 million. This followed earlier strong statements that ruled out any devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Economists, including the World Bank, believe foreign speculators have ignored the fundamental strength of Indonesia's booming economy. \par \par \uc2  Bankers have said Indonesia's total foreign debt, with less than 50 percent held by the private sector, currently stands at around $95 billion. \par \par \uc2  About 40 percent of the debt is denominated in Japanese yen. Indonesia has never defaulted on or rescheduled its debt payments. \par \par \uc2  Murdiono said Suharto -- believed to pay special attention to Indonesia's foreign debt and inflation rate -- always watched economic developments closely . \par \par \uc2  Murdiono also joined the country's top economic ministers in stressing that Indonesia, Asia's only member of the Organisation of Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC), would not devalue the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "The government does not see any reason for it (a devaluation). The situation in 1986 is very different. The oil price dropped sharply to below $10 a barrel from $30 at that time. But now it is different," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have said the foreign financial community has painful memories of Indonesia's two devaluations in the 1980s; in 1983 and 1986. \par \par \uc2  Murdiono also said the government was committed to maintaining its free \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system, which he said was vital to attract badly needed foreign investment. \par \par \uc2  "This has been our policy since the beginning of development. The government is convinced that this is the correct step," he added. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , raised by half a percentage point the interest rate on short-term securities (SBPUs) of all maturities on Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers, who said the move would help support the rupiah, said it was also aimed at stopping players from taking advantage of interest rate differentials. \par \par \uc2  Surat Berharga Pasar Uang (SBPUs) are short-term securities bought by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to inject additional liquidity into the banking system. \par \par \uc2  But one money market dealer said the hike was not enough to reduce short-term interest rate differentials between the key discount rates and forward premiums. \par \par \uc2  "The move was positive but players can still utilise \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  facilities to buy dollars because of attractive margins on forward premiums," he said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr1g0707j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
