\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah/Rates/Amplifier -2: Inflation Caution \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 1995\par 12:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar last week surged on the back of unfounded speculation that the rupiah would be devalued, as in Mexico, in the wake of investor bearishness toward emerging markets after the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  International fund managers unwound their positions in Indonesian equities and short-term securities, dealers said, sending the rupiah on a decline and spurring heavy dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  The short-term outflow of funds is seen as 'only a very temporary move, initiated by international fund managers,' said Patrice Meda, president director of PT Indosuez Indonesia Bank. 'It was an emotional reaction to what happened in Mexico. Too fast a parallel was drawn with Indonesia overseas.' \par \par \uc2  As fund managers exited, speculators apparently smelled opportunity, Meda said. \par \par \uc2  'They were trying to make money on a possible devaluation, but it was just some fund managers closing their positions,' he said. 'That was enough to disturb the market.' \par \par \uc2  On Friday Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars and on Saturday officials vowed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. On Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , raised by 0.50 percentage point the interest rates of its Sertifikat Bank Indonesia (SBI), and its short-term money market security, Surat Berharga Pasar Uang (SBPU), by the same amount. \par \par \uc2  Although the hikes cooled the dollar further to 2,214 rupiah from its opening at 2,220 rupiah, and was seen as a signal of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  defense, dealers said it was part of the government's policy of controlling inflation, at 9.6% year-on-year as of December, and tightening rupiah liquidity. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-01-95 \par \par \uc2  1141GMT \par \par \uc2  1140 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr1g0053o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
