\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Vows  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  To Support Rupiah: Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By PETER HALESWORTH \par \uc2 148 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1995\par 12:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-DJ)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities have taken up arms in what they say is a 'war of nerves' waged by offshore speculators against the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Two top monetary authorities vowed Saturday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sell possibly hundreds of millions of U.S. dollars to defend the home \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  While Jakarta \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said Friday's estimated four \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to sell 200 million to 300 million dlrs may have grounded the dollar for now, officials showed no signs of relaxing heading into the new week. \par \par \uc2  'We will challenge the speculators. We will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling the dollar in the forward and spot markets at the right time,' Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-01-95 \par \par \uc2  1122GMT \par \par \uc2  1134 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr1e0045z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
