\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah withstands foreign pressure. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 13 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah stabilised against the dollar following concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday after a week-long attack by offshore banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to have calmed down nervous trading conditions, at least temporarily. \par \par \uc2  "It was a good move from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Finally it has shown its teeth," one private bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold spot dollars, outrights and swaps in the market to kill devaluation rumours, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled the dollar down to stabilise at around 2,219/19 rupiah from a day's high of 2,235 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move was quite positive. They want to show foreign speculators that they want to maintain that exchange rate," said an economist who asked not to be named. \par \par \uc2  Other analysts said the week-long dumping of the rupiah was an overreaction which had not been backed by fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's coordinating minister for the economy Saleh Afiff said on Thursday that the rupiah was competitive and ruled out any devaluation. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign fund managers view Asian and Latin American countries together as emerging markets," the economist, who works with a U.S. investment house, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "In fact Asia is very different from Latin America. Asia is politically more stable and economic fundamentals are much sounder," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Why compare the two together?" he asked. \par \par \uc2  Other analysts added that Indonesia's current account deficit accounts for only two percent of the gross domestic product. They said the huge debt is not viewed as a problem as long as non-oil exports continue to grow, and provided there are no external shocks. \par \par \uc2  The attack on the rupiah started last Friday in the United States on fears over Indonesia's large foreign debt, but the intensity rose on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The inflow of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings should be able to repay the debt obligation of interest and principal," the economist said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers who had been waiting for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move after the dollar rose above the bank's band, welcomed the move saying it would help stabilise the market. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr1d08982\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
