\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  stabilises rupiah for now. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 488 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Jan 13 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah stabilised against the dollar after strong \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday following a week-long attack launched by offshore banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to have calmed nervous trading conditions, at least temporarily. \par \par \uc2  "It was a good move from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Finally it has shown its teeth," one private bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold spot dollars, outrights and swaps in the market to kill devaluation rumours, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled the dollar down to stabilise around 2,219/19 rupiah in late afternoon from a day's high of 2,235 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move was quite positive. They want to show foreign speculators they want to maintain that exchange rate," one economist with a U.S. investment bank said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also maintained its fixing rate at 2,188/2,218 at 0800 GMT despite heavy foreign pressure, which analysts saw as a strong signal of its commitment to a firm gradual depreciation policy. \par \par \uc2  "The fixing and the earlier \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has calmed down the market," one foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Economists classified the week-long selling of the rupiah as an overreaction not backed by fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Indonesian coordinating minister for economy Saleh Afiff said Thursday the rupiah was competitive and ruled out any devaluation. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign fund managers view Asian and Latin American countries together as emerging markets," the investment bank economist said. \par \par \uc2  "In fact Asia is very different from Latin America. Asia is politically more stable and economic fundamentals are much sounder," the economist said. \par \par \uc2  "Why compare the two together?" he asked. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the Indonesian current account deficit accounted for only two percent of GDP and the huge debt, expected to hit $100 billion in 1995/96, would not be a problem as long as non-oil exports can continue to grow and provided there are no external shocks. \par \par \uc2  "They are only the same in the category that they are developing countries. It is a poor generalisation," the U.S. investment bank economist said. \par \par \uc2  "The whole story will not stop yet. Some speculators will further test the resistance of exotic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The attack on the rupiah started last Friday in the U.S. on fears over Indonesia's large foreign debt, but the intensity increased on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The stock market was plunging too because of the Mexico crisis. It think it may continue for some time. But all this is not backed by fundamentals," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The inflow of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings should be able to repay the debt obligation of interest and principal," one economist said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers who had been waiting for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move after the dollar rose above the bank's band, welcomed the move saying it would help stabilise the market. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011